  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given function should be in the form of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>So, for travelling wave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;should be linear function of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>and&nbsp;should be finite and continuous for all values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> linear function in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>",
